{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) and it has about 310 GB free out of 512 GB, roughly 60% free, so it isn't actually low on space. The Windows warning may be out of date or may refer to a different drive. If you'd like to free up some room anyway, empty your Recycle Bin and Downloads folder, then open Settings > System > Storage and remove the temporary files. If the warning keeps appearing after that, reply to this ticket and we'll look further.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up user (Dana Whitfield, CEO, VIP, active, not blocked). Only device is BL-LT-0101 (Windows 11 Pro, online, last check-in 2026-10-11). check_device_status shows disk 512 GB total, 310 GB free, percent_free 60.5, no warnings. KB-017 threshold is under 10% free, so the device does not meet the low-disk condition and the escalation criterion does not apply. No cleanup was performed remotely; the KB-017 fix steps are user-side, so I gave them as optional self-help. Possible causes for the Windows message: stale notification, or a different volume/drive. If the user reports the warning again, check which drive Windows names and consider a fresh check of device status. No actions queued.",
